We also, we just simply
shot this in one angle.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.340
Straight-on angle, and I shot it in 4k.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.110
Most of our phones in this
room actually shoot 4k.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.500
And then I edited it at 1080p project.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.070
I know that probably flew
over some people's heads.

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:50.620
Essentially, I filmed it
really high resolution,

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.240
and then I edited it at
a smaller resolution,

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.890
so it makes it look like
we have multiple angles.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.240
And I'll show you an
example in just a second.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.980
Then we captured the
audio on a Zoom recorder.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.170
Edited each episode straight through.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:03.637
This alleviated the headache.

00:11:03.637 --> 00:11:07.360
We're not trying to cut
videos or cut content

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.000
so it came over quickly.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.287
It was just like, "All right, ready?

00:11:10.287 --> 00:11:11.127
"All right, here we go.

00:11:11.127 --> 00:11:13.267
"Start the show, hit record.

00:11:13.267 --> 00:11:15.280
"And then end the show, hit record."

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.410
And then the edit was just that simple.

