00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.270
Tips for your first episode.

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:49.970
Just some tips for your first
episode of your podcast.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.710
The strategy aspect of things.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.670
So, when we first started the podcast,

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:58.620
he wanted to share, Mike
wanted to share the story

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.850
of how they came to where they are.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.187
And so he's like, "Dude,
let's title this podcast

00:15:03.187 --> 00:15:04.277
"The Struggle is Real,

00:15:04.277 --> 00:15:06.199
"'cause that's, man,
the struggle is real."

00:15:06.199 --> 00:15:07.032
And I was like, "That's dope,

00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:09.020
"but nobody's searching
the struggle is real."

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.097
Right?

00:15:10.097 --> 00:15:12.510
So I went on YouTube.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.370
And I saw that people were searching

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:16.870
how to start a lash
business with no money.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.080
Which essentially was their story,

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.320
so that was the title
of their video that we,

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.433
of the first,

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.720
their first podcast that they put out.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.720
And we did the research.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.360
That's simply research before
you press record, right?

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.680
And so do the research.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.750
Your podcasts could be reverse engineered.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.360
So don't just go out there and talk about

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:37.460
what you wanna talk about.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.160
See, based off of what
you wanna talk about,

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.600
go ahead and search what you wanna search,

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.570
and see what people are searching.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.520
And you can learn all this through VRA.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:51.020
We learned that probably
when you start off,

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:53.160
you wanna start with volume.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.530
So, we started with eight
podcasts for the first two months.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:58.570
So, we dropped two episodes
every week for every month.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.250
That may sound like a lot for you guys,

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.850
but I would actually disagree,

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.530
because we shot those all in one day.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.300
And power tip to them, power tip to me.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.660
But at the same time, it's doable.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:14.613
Just hunker down and
get 'er done. (laughs)

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.101
I don't know why I said that, okay.

00:16:18.101 --> 00:16:19.240
(Omar laughs)

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.220
Okay.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.110
And then another thing
that they did up front,

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:22.943
and it's something you can do,

00:16:22.943 --> 00:16:24.840
is they did a giveaway every episode.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:27.560
So, it was about a month-long giveaway,

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.360
and when they announced the
winner the following episode,

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:31.530
they started a new giveaway,

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.320
and it increased shareability,

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.400
it grew the email list for the podcast.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:38.163
But you can give away
something during the episode.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.070
Another thing is, this may
be obvious, may be not be,

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:44.940
but post your podcasts.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.720
If you film 'em, if you record them,

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:50.860
post them on YouTube, and
post them to podcasts.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.220
You create the standard

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.387
for what your audience expects from you.

00:16:56.232 --> 00:16:59.890
I think this is powerful,
because I wrote it.

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.185
I'm just kidding.

00:17:01.185 --> 00:17:02.060
(audience laughs)

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.920
Wow, Omar, chill, bro.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:05.270
Ah, no, it's fresh, though.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.180
What I mean by that is
because we started off

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.790
with long-form content,

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:13.780
people met them with long-form content,

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:16.220
and nobody will expect less from you.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:19.710
And so, with every episode
being about 15 minutes,

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:23.240
sometimes 20, sometimes 12,
nobody's expecting less.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.960
I would actually say on Think Media,

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.230
we're fighting for attention,

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.550
because it's different kinds of content,

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.570
but we also didn't start off this way.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.730
So, if you have yet to start,

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:36.220
it's not a bad idea to start
with longer-form content,

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.970
because if people stumble on your stuff,

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:40.893
find value, they won't expect
anything less from you.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.493
Thank you.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.030
So, what are some lessons
we learned so far?

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.010
Number one, that there's
a massive opportunity

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:52.910
for your business and brand
to be on a, have a podcast.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:55.090
Secondly is that there's
a people waiting for you.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.320
I think sometimes we forget that.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.910
We make it all about us.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:00.190
Like, I don't have this, I look like this,

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:02.995
but legit, there's people
waiting for content

00:18:02.995 --> 00:18:06.410
that is coming from your perspective,

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:09.670
coming from your experiences,
and things like that.

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.210
And so, think about the people.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.004
I think that alleviates
the pressure altogether

00:18:14.004 --> 00:18:16.790
in the sense that there
is a group of people

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:18.140
that need this stuff.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:19.840
I need to get it into their hands.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.340
Podcasts can be monetized.

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:23.173
We definitely learned that.

00:18:23.173 --> 00:18:25.370
I would say before I tapped into the world

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.489
of online marketing and
networking and stuff

00:18:27.489 --> 00:18:31.480
that I always thought podcasts
were such a free thing,

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.890
and the way we monetize this, obviously,

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.528
is they have the supply chain.

00:18:35.528 --> 00:18:39.670
This can also be monetized
if they wanna sell ad space

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:40.983
on their podcasts.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.160
We actually, though, use it, they use it

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:46.320
for their own promotion.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.453
So they self-promote.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:50.120
Which you notice.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:51.782
They promote their classes on there,

00:18:51.782 --> 00:18:54.570
and they promote speaking engagements.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.651
They've also been invited to
speak at LashCon this October,

00:18:57.651 --> 00:18:59.513
which is pretty crazy.

00:19:00.613 --> 00:19:04.240
(audience applauds)

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.680
And why is it so important
for your business?

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:10.130
Raise your hand if you
struggle with consistency.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.270
Let's get it, everybody in the room.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:16.400
This is an easy way of
getting content done.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.060
One-shot angle, talk straight through

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.980
if you have your points dialed in maybe,

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.590
or maybe you just have the general idea

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:23.423
of what you wanna talk about,

00:19:23.423 --> 00:19:26.380
but again, if you're just
starting off, just go for it.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:27.930
It doesn't have to be polished.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.110
Another reason is 'cause
it gives you the ability

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.420
to repurpose the content,

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:33.440
which Sean just talked about.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.380
Like, you can cut up five
pieces of micro content

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.710
from your podcast episode,

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.380
not having to ever sit down
again in front of the camera,

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.720
but because it's shot, it's put together,

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:46.460
you can now dish out
content on other platforms.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.870
And then it also builds trust.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:50.770
I think the coolest thing

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.830
is they just haven't had to sell anything.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.537
They're just like, "Yo,
this is how you do stuff.

00:19:54.537 --> 00:19:55.837
"This is what we've experienced.

00:19:55.837 --> 00:19:59.930
"This is how we do our
things here at our company."

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.867
And it's that jab jab, right hook

00:20:01.867 --> 00:20:03.800
from Gary V. mentality,

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.740
where if they really
wanna ask, they'll ask,

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.410
but they actually don't need to.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.410
But when they do, it's gonna be awesome,

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.243
because people are gonna be like,

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:12.367
"For sure, we'll go to that live event,

00:20:12.367 --> 00:20:14.257
"because we've been following
you guys for two years,

00:20:14.257 --> 00:20:15.170
"I can't wait to come here."

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:17.150
And I think there's a
handful of us here right now

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.260
because Sean has hit you a little bit

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.473
with the jab jabs.

00:20:21.532 --> 00:20:22.365
Sorry.

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:28.480
Oh, another good reason is
you reach two types of people.

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:30.460
Simply making a video podcast,

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.320
you reach two types of people.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:32.600
People who listen to podcasts,

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.143
and people who are on YouTube.

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:37.197
You hack watch-listen times,

00:20:37.197 --> 00:20:38.730
simply what I talked about,

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.630
that just because it's longer form,

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.280
you get to win on that end.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.596
And then here's just a legit stat

00:20:45.596 --> 00:20:49.750
that there's over 500 million
active users on YouTube,

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.980
versus less than one million podcasts.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.380
So that's just a number to keep in mind

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.960
that shows that there's so
much opportunity in this phase.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:01.217
So, conclusion, start podcasting now.

00:21:01.217 --> 00:21:02.050
(audience cheers)

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.523
Make some noise if you
gonna start your podcast.

00:21:03.523 --> 00:21:05.030
(audience cheers and applauds)

